  "orientation": {
    "knockdown": "heavy = siRNA against the PRMT, light = control siRNA: \"Light and heavy labeled cells were transfected with control siRNA and siRNA specifically targeting PRMT4, 5 or 7, respectively\" (Methods, Cell labeling by SILAC); \"SILAC labeled wild-type (light) or PRMT7-knockdown (heavy) cells (Fig. 1d)\" (Results). The lists' ratio (siPRMTx/siCTL) is the export's Abundance Ratio (Heavy)/(Light) of the same peptide group",
    "inhibitor": "heavy = SGC3027, light = untreated, as the paper reads its SGC3027 lists (\"Upon SGC3027 treatment, 503 MMA sites ... had at least two-fold reduction\"; the listed ratios are the export's H/L). The Methods sentence \"light and heavy labeled cells were treated with or without SGC3027, respectively\" read literally says the reverse; the list headers say siPRMT7/siCTL (copied from SD1). See sgc3027_orientation_check"
  },
  "log2_treated_control": "log2 of the export's Abundance Ratio (Heavy)/(Light) (of the listed ratio for list-only peptides)",
  "normalisation": "None applied here. The export's Abundance Ratio (Heavy)/(Light) is Proteome Discoverer 2.2's (its normalisation settings are not stated). The lists add a protein-level ratio from a separate proteome and the \"normalized ratio\" = methylation ratio / protein ratio; the paper calls on the methylation ratio and uses the normalised one only to say how many changes protein levels explain (25 PRMT7 sites)",
  "replicates": "Not stated in the paper for the SILAC methylomes. SD1 holds two exports, \"repeat 1\" (raw files siPRMT7-Methylation-SILAC-1 to 10 and -Dimethylation-SILAC-1 to 5, as 15 light/heavy sample pairs) and \"repeat 2\" (AD293-sIPRMT7-SILAC-..., one sample pair); the PRMT7 lists come from repeat 1 only. SD3 and SD5 hold one export each (one light/heavy sample pair)",
  "adjusted_p": "Proteome Discoverer 2.2 \"Abundance Ratio Adj. P-Value: (Heavy) / (Light)\" of SD1 and SD3, as given; the paper does not describe it. Each export compares one SILAC pair of cultures (SD1 repeat 1 enters its 15 raw files as 15 sample pairs), so it is not a test over biological replicates. SD5 gives none. Every peptide group at the 0.01 floor (and at the 100 ceiling) has the same adjusted p within an export, so every abolished peptide passes the uniform rule: PRMT7_si [3.7647591725804e-17]; PRMT7_si_rep2 [4.85056113408151e-17]; PRMT7_SGC3027 [3.63233724653148e-17]",
  "paper_rule": "\"297 MMA sites from 174 proteins had at least a two-fold reduction in mono-methylation signals\" and \"methylation at 176 MMA sites from 108 proteins was completely abolished when PRMT7 was knocked down\" (Results); sheet names \"(FC>2)\" and \"(abolished)\"; no statistical test is stated for the ratios",
  "source_rule": "peptide H/L < 0.5 (more than twofold lower with the perturbation): decreased; abolished at the Proteome Discoverer floor H/L = 0.01. Site: decreased when the paper's lists (FC>2 or abolished, me1 or me2) name it, no_significant_change when a quantified peptide in the lists' scope carries it",
  "uniform_rule": "peptide log2 treated/control <= -1 (decreased) or >= 1 (increased) with the export's adjusted p < 0.05; sites by scripts/peptide_calls.site_response (strict)",
  "boundary": {
    "groups_at_H/L_0.5": [
      "PRMT7_SGC3027 Q96G74 RGGGVGVGGGGTGVGGGDRDR 1xMethyl [R1] H/L=0.5 listed=False",
      "PRMT4_si Q8TD08 PSGRGAAPSLTSQAAAQVANQALIR 1xMethyl [R4] H/L=0.5 listed=False"
    ],
    "reading": "sheet names say FC>2 and the one group at exactly 0.5 whose site is listed by no other group is not listed: H/L < 0.5"
  },
